{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Lest there be among you a root bearing gall and wormwood.</b> Poison-gall (ראש) is called ראש, 'head,' because it is the head of all bitter things, and it is more bitter than all the rest — *toxigue* in the vernacular. And there are those who explained that it is called ראש because the poison is found in the head of the viper. And the term לענה (wormwood) is a species of herb, from the root of (Numbers 30): לענות נפש — 'to afflict the soul' — for it is utter affliction of the soul."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The Romance gloss טוסיג\"י corresponds to Old Provençal/Old French *toxigue* ('poison'); transcribed as found."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:52.682963989Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}